-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "means" definition, a "where", "if", "unless",
--                "upon" or "at" not met, a period fixed in the text's own words and missed).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a class described by "who", a lifted bar that grants
--                nothing, a bare "must" not done).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- The Land Titles (Strata) Act and the Building Maintenance and Strata Management Act are not among the sources:
-- their facts are inputs.  PERIODS are counted under O 3 r 3 (lines 323 to 329); the last day is the seam input
-- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.

