    `o 49 r 6(2)(b) an order declaring that the originating application has not been duly served on the defendant`
    `o 49 r 6(2)(c) the discharge of any order giving permission to serve the originating application on the defendant out of Singapore`
    `o 49 r 6(2)(d) the discharge of any order extending the validity of the originating application for the purpose of service`
    `o 49 r 6(2)(e) the protection or release of any property of the defendant seized or threatened with seizure in the proceedings`
    `o 49 r 6(2)(f) the discharge of any order made to prevent any dealing with any property of the defendant`
    `o 49 r 6(2)(g) a declaration that the Court has no jurisdiction over the defendant in respect of the subject matter of the claim or the relief or remedy sought`
    `o 49 r 6(2)(h) such other relief as may be appropriate`

-- COVERS O 49 r 6(2)
-- src:6404 | (2) The reliefs mentioned in paragraph (1) are — ( a )
-- src:6405 | an order setting aside the originating application or service of the originating application on the defendant;
-- src:6406 | ( b )
-- src:6407 | an order declaring that the originating application has not been duly served on the defendant;
-- src:6408 | ( c )
-- src:6409 | the discharge of any order giving permission to serve the originating application on the defendant out of Singapore;
-- src:6410 | ( d )
-- src:6411 | the discharge of any order extending the validity of the originating application for the purpose of service;
-- src:6412 | ( e )
-- src:6413 | the protection or release of any property of the defendant seized or threatened with seizure in the proceedings;
-- src:6414 | ( f )
-- src:6415 | the discharge of any order made to prevent any dealing with any property of the defendant;
-- src:6416 | ( g )
-- src:6417 | a declaration that in the circumstances of the case the Court has no jurisdiction over the defendant in respect of the subject matter of the claim or the relief or remedy sought in the action; or
-- src:6418 | ( h )
-- src:6419 | such other relief as may be appropriate.
@ref O 49 r 6(2) (src:6404-6419)
GIVEN relief IS A `o 49 r 6(2) the relief`
      `the other relief is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 49 r 6(2) the relief is one mentioned in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    IF relief EQUALS `o 49 r 6(2)(h) such other relief as may be appropriate`
    THEN
        IF `the other relief is appropriate`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such other relief as may be appropriate" is limited by appropriateness
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS O 49 r 6(3)
-- JUDGMENT QB | O 49 r 6(3) | NOTHING when the application under paragraph (1) is not made by summons with a verifying affidavit served with it | JUST FALSE for the compliance question, with consequence functions staying NOTHING
-- src:6420 | (3) An application under paragraph (1) must be made by summons supported by an affidavit verifying the facts on which the application is based and a copy of the affidavit must be served with the summons.
@ref O 49 r 6(3) (src:6420)
GIVEN `it is an application under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `it is supported by an affidavit verifying the facts on which it is based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the affidavit is served with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 49 r 6(3) the application is made by summons supported by an affidavit as it must be` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is an application under paragraph (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "An application under paragraph (1)"
        IF document EQUALS `Summons` AND `it is supported by an affidavit verifying the facts on which it is based` AND `a copy of the affidavit is served with the summons`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must be made by summons supported by an affidavit" is a bare "must"; what follows non-compliance is O 3 r 2(4), not here

-- "Upon the hearing": the power arises when the hearing takes place.
-- COVERS O 49 r 6(4)
-- src:6421 | (4) Upon the hearing of an application under paragraph (1), the Court may make such order as the Court thinks fit and may give such directions for its disposal as may be appropriate, including directions for the trial thereof as a preliminary issue.
@ref O 49 r 6(4) (src:6421)
GIVEN `the application under paragraph (1) is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 49 r 6(4) the Court may make such order and give such directions as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the application under paragraph (1) is being heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the hearing of an application under paragraph (1)" is an "upon" condition

