`o 49 r 7 the Court may by order give such directions as to the proceedings to be taken as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `it is the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which this Order relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which this Order relates" is an "at" condition
